# Final fallback only: copy beside the private --config file as .env, owned by
# the executing user with mode 0600; keep the parent directory private (0700).
# Do not paste real values into chat, commands, YAML, logs, or this example.
# Remove upload/staging copies after securely installing the private file.
# Existing process variables win, even when empty. For each proxy case pair, if
# either spelling exists in the original process, both file spellings are ignored.
# If neither exists in the process, both file spellings retain native precedence.
# No cwd/parent-directory search.
#
# Literal UTF-8 without BOM: one NAME=VALUE per line (LF or CRLF); blank/full-line # comments
# are ignored. Optional `export ` prefix and matching single/double quotes are
# accepted. Unquoted surrounding whitespace is trimmed; quoted spaces remain.
# Matching outer quotes are removed; interior quote characters remain literal.
# No variable expansion, command substitution, escape processing, or multiline
# values. A # within a value is literal, not an inline comment. Duplicate names,
# malformed assignments, a missing closing outer quote, and NUL are errors.
# Never shell-source.
# All assignments below are commented out so this file contains no credentials.

# Repository passwords: THE NAMES ARE DEFINED BY YAML password_env, NOT THE CLI.
# Use the exact names from repositories.shared.password_env and
# repositories.bot.password_env; authorized peers use their registry password_env.
# Example only, if YAML selects these names:
# HUB_SHARED_PASSWORD=
# HUB_BOT_PASSWORD=
# Each selected value becomes RESTIC_PASSWORD only in that repository's child.
# RESTIC_PASSWORD itself is an input only if YAML explicitly chooses that name.
# Forwarded connection/system names and the three AWS credential names below are
# reserved and cannot be password_env names in active config/registry entries,
# regardless of storage provider. Use dedicated password names instead.

# R2 storage credentials (not required for storage.provider: local).
# AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
# AWS_SESSION_TOKEN=

# Connection variables forwarded to acquisition curl and restic.
# HTTPS_PROXY=
# HTTP_PROXY=
# ALL_PROXY=
# NO_PROXY=
# https_proxy=
# http_proxy=
# all_proxy=
# no_proxy=
# Prefer HTTPS_PROXY/https_proxy for HTTPS endpoints. curl ignores HTTP_PROXY;
# ALL_PROXY/all_proxy are curl fallbacks, not restic HTTP(S) proxy replacements.

# Trusted CA paths (absolute). curl and restic retain their own TLS semantics.
# SSL_CERT_FILE=
# SSL_CERT_DIR=
# CURL_CA_BUNDLE=
# CURL_CA_BUNDLE is curl-specific; use SSL_CERT_FILE/SSL_CERT_DIR for restic.

# Native restic TLS filenames: forwarded only to storage restic, never curl.
# RESTIC_CACERT=
# RESTIC_TLS_CLIENT_CERT=
# Keep a TLS client certificate/private-key file private as well.

# Executable lookup/platform context retained from the parent environment.
# Normally already set by the host and unnecessary in .env. Never put secrets here.
# PATH=
# SYSTEMROOT=
# WINDIR=

# Child values controlled by the CLI, not configurable through .env:
# LANG=C.UTF-8, LC_ALL=C.UTF-8, TZ=UTC;
# TMPDIR, TMP, TEMP (restic gets its private state temp directory);
# RESTIC_PASSWORD (mapped from the selected YAML password_env).
# Other RESTIC_* controls, HOME, XDG_* and arbitrary ambient variables are not
# forwarded. Configure repository, cache, retries, and paths in YAML/the CLI.
# Secret-provider bootstrap tokens belong to its launcher; the CLI does not use
# them. Optional utsurigi-memory is a separate program and does not load this file.
